**Definition 3.2 (the complete source operation, including earlier failure).**
For any prescribed double-wall path starting at $a$, put

$$
\begin{aligned}
\lambda(t)&=\frac{(k'(t))_+}{k(t)}+
             \frac{(-k'(t))_+}{c-k(t)},\qquad
S(t)=\exp\!\left(-\int_0^t\lambda(s)\,ds\right),\\
K_t&=\sqrt{S(t)}\operatorname{diag}_i
 \left(\sqrt{p_i(k(t))/p_i(a)}e^{-iH_i(t)}\right),\\
g_i(t)&=\lambda(t)-(\log p_i(k(t)))',\qquad
J_i(t)=\sqrt{g_i(t)}\,|f\rangle\langle i|K_t.
\end{aligned}
\tag{FH.5}
$$

These are the credited canonical operations. The rates are nonnegative
almost everywhere: the logarithmic probability derivatives are
$k'/k,-k'/(c-k),0$, and $\lambda$ is their maximum. Compact strict
support and absolute continuity make all rates integrable. The squared
modulus of the $i$th diagonal entry of $K_t$ has derivative
$-g_i(t)|(K_t)_{ii}|^2$. Integrating proves

$$
K_T^\dagger K_T+\sum_{i=0}^4\int_0^T J_i(t)^\dagger J_i(t)\,dt=I_5.
\tag{FH.6}
$$

For every actual conditional joint input $\rho^h_{AR}$, including arbitrary
archive/reference correlations, the terminal live output is
$(K_T\otimes I_R)\rho^h_{AR}(K_T^\dagger\otimes I_R)$.
Failure on a Borel set $E$ in original mode $i$ is

$$
\int_E(J_i(t)\otimes I_R)\rho^h_{AR}
              (J_i(t)^\dagger\otimes I_R)\,dt,
\tag{FH.7}
$$

with the actual first timestamp, mode and $f$. Retain source/epoch,
preparation, request, reference, calibration, permissions and all updates
jointly. Integrate these branch maps against the same actual history
distribution if histories are mixed. The mathematical source label $h$
in this expression is not delivered to the controller. Already stopped
inputs retain their old event and stopped successor. Equations
(FH.5)–(FH.7) describe every branch of the six-unit preparation too;
an unsuccessful preparation is never retried or silently removed.

